Subject: [PATCH] main: call adw_init() before creating the application

KgxApplication's instance init calls adw_style_manager_get_default(),
and main() calls gtk_window_set_default_icon_name(), both before
GtkApplication::startup runs gtk_init(). With GTK 4.22 this aborts:

  Gdk-ERROR: gdk_display_manager_get() was called before gtk_init()

Initialise libadwaita (and thus GTK) at the top of main().

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/src/main.c	2026-11-15 18:32:50.389110494 +0100
+++ b/src/main.c	2026-11-15 18:32:50.403927137 +0100
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@
 
 #include <glib/gi18n.h>
 #include <locale.h>
+#include <adwaita.h>
 #include <kgx.h>
 
 int
@@ -31,6 +32,10 @@
   bind_textdomain_codeset (GETTEXT_PACKAGE, "UTF-8");
   textdomain (GETTEXT_PACKAGE);
 
+  /* GTK >= 4.22 aborts if GDK is used before gtk_init(); KgxApplication
+   * touches AdwStyleManager in its init, so initialise libadwaita first. */
+  adw_init ();
+
   g_set_prgname (KGX_BIN_NAME);
   g_set_application_name (KGX_DISPLAY_NAME);
   gtk_window_set_default_icon_name (KGX_APPLICATION_ID);
